Abstract
Booking bus tickets manually at a counter takes time and often leads to mistakes such as the same seat being given to two people. This project presents a console-based Bus Reservation System developed in C. It provides a menu-driven interface that allows an operator to register passengers, view available buses and fares, check which seats are free, book a seat, cancel a ticket with a refund, and generate a complete booking report. The system handles three buses with 20 seats each, calculates the fare automatically based on the passenger’s age (child and senior citizen concessions), and saves all data in a file so that the information is not lost when the program is closed.
Problem Statement
Traditional paper-based or manual bus ticket booking has several drawbacks:
Difficulty in quickly knowing which seats are still available in a bus.
The same seat can be given to two passengers by mistake (double booking).
Human error in calculating the fare, especially for children and senior citizens.
Cancelling a ticket and freeing the seat needs manual updating of records.
Preparing a booking report at the end of the day is slow and tedious.
Solution: This automated C application replaces manual registers with structured arrays and files, ensuring fast seat lookup, error-free fare calculation, protection against double booking, and instant reports.
Objectives
1. To automate passenger registration and generate a unique Passenger ID.
2. To display the available buses, their routes and fares.
3. To show seat availability of a bus and prevent a booked seat from being booked again.
4. To calculate the fare automatically with a 50% concession for children (below 12 years) and 30% for senior citizens (60 years and above).
5. To allow ticket cancellation, free the seat again and calculate the refund after a 10% cancellation charge.
6. To generate a booking report with ticket status and total collection.
7. To store all records permanently in a file using file handling in C.
