Algorithm
1. Start the program, initialize the 3 buses with all seats free, and load saved data from bus_data.dat (if the file exists).
2. Display the Main Menu containing options 1 to 6 and 0 for Exit.
3. Read the user’s choice.
4. Use a switch statement to execute the corresponding function:
Case 1 (Passenger Registration): Check if space is available. Read name, age, gender and phone. Assign the next Passenger ID, store the record and save to file.
Case 2 (Book Seat): Read Passenger ID and check that the passenger exists. Show the buses, read the bus number, display the seats and read the seat number. If the seat is free, calculate the fare, generate a ticket number, mark the seat as booked, save to file and print the ticket; otherwise display an error.
Case 3 (Cancel Ticket): Read the ticket number and search for it. If it exists and is active, mark it as cancelled, free the seat, calculate the refund (90% of fare) and save to file.
Case 4 (Check Seat Availability): Read the bus number, display all 20 seats as free or booked and print the count of available seats.
Case 5 (View Buses & Fares): Display the list of buses with route and base fare.
Case 6 (Booking Report): Loop through all tickets and print the details with status (Booked / Cancelled), then print the total booked, total cancelled and total collection.
Case 0 (Exit): Terminate the program loop (return 0).
5. Repeat the menu loop until the user chooses to exit.
6. Stop.
